1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:04,975
Part fifteen. PM Surya Ghar subsidy and solar loans.

2
00:00:05,810 --> 00:00:08,530
Open Subsidy and add an application.

3
00:00:08,530 --> 00:00:10,042
Choose the customer.

4
00:00:10,042 --> 00:00:12,157
The scheme is PM Surya Ghar.

5
00:00:12,157 --> 00:00:16,162
Type the application number from the national portal.

6
00:00:17,050 --> 00:00:22,951
Leave capacity and amount empty: the capacity comes from the customer's project,

7
00:00:22,951 --> 00:00:25,311
and the subsidy from the scheme.

8
00:00:25,311 --> 00:00:31,138
Thirty thousand rupees per kilowatt up to two, eighteen thousand for the third,

9
00:00:31,138 --> 00:00:33,424
at most seventy-eight thousand.

10
00:00:33,424 --> 00:00:37,628
North-East, hill states and islands get ten percent more.

11
00:00:38,530 --> 00:00:45,189
Tick the documents as you submit them: Aadhaar, electricity bill, bank passbook,

12
00:00:45,189 --> 00:00:49,933
site photo, net meter agreement and commissioning report.

13
00:00:49,933 --> 00:00:50,349
Save.

14
00:00:51,250 --> 00:00:57,574
Update the status as the portal moves: documents verified, under review, approved,

15
00:00:57,574 --> 00:00:58,346
disbursed.

16
00:00:58,346 --> 00:01:03,436
Applications pending for more than forty-five days show in alerts.

17
00:01:03,436 --> 00:01:07,138
The subsidy goes to the customer's bank account.

18
00:01:08,050 --> 00:01:14,181
For customers buying on a loan, open Solar Loans and add one: the bank, amount,

19
00:01:14,181 --> 00:01:16,121
interest rate and tenure.

20
00:01:16,121 --> 00:01:22,330
The monthly EMI is worked out for you, and you track the status to disbursement.

21
00:01:24,020 --> 00:01:28,077
Next video: Service tickets and AMC contracts.

